aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}8x=2\\lambda x \\\\ 4y=\\lambda (2y-2)\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}x(4-\\lambda )=0 \\\\ y(\\lambda -2)=\\lambda \\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we break it up into several cases:\n\n- Assuming $x=0$ in the first equation of the system, the constraint condition ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2y=0$ implies\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-2y & =0\\,⇒\\,y=0,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the critical points $(0,0),(0,2).$\n\n- Assuming $\\lambda =4$ in the first equation of the system, the second equation of the system implies\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(4-2)=4\\,⇒\\,y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the constraint condition ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2y=0$ implies\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the critical point $(0,2).$\n\nTherefore, $f$ has possible extreme values at the points\n\n$$\n(0,0),\\,(0,2).\n$$\n\nWe evaluate $f$ at these points. These are given in the following table:\n\n| $(x,y)$ | $(0,0)$ | $(0,2)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x,y)$ | $5$ | $13$ |\n\nTherefore, the function reaches a maximum value at the point $(0,2)$ and its maximum value is $13.$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186129085 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386312 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186129136 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387463 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186129136 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387470 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186129136 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387477 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186129137 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387484 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186129140 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387857 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186129140 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387864 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186129161 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387497 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186129161 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387504 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186129194 1038 #edb/r