76" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386005 1081 "images/17/177ca7f40ef24cf2f45a15b78487700d1f0efd094c975079cf4704b46debefb1.png" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386005 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386005 1084 #uuid "2ecd37a8-72a0-57e0-80f3-347934775efa" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386006 1068 #edb/ref 17592186386007 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386006 1069 "q-7798" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386006 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386006 1071 "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-8{y}^{′}+16y=0,\\,y(1)=2,\\text{ }\\text{ }{y}^{′}(1)=-1.\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386006 1072 #uuid "e0ccd8f3-5c55-5b1e-8569-1f7045c0f609" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386006 1074 "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-8\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+16{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda +16) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda +16 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -4) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\lambda =4$ is a repeated root.\n\nSo the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{4x}+Bx{e}^{4x}.\n$$\n\nLet us find constants $A$ and $B.$ \n\nSubstituting $y(1)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA{e}^{4}+B{e}^{4}=2.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=-1.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=4A{e}^{4x}+B{e}^{4x}+4Bx{e}^{4x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=1$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n4A{e}^{4}+5B{e}^{4}=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following system of equations for $A$ and $B$:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}A{e}^{4}+B{e}^{4}=2 \\\\ 4A{e}^{4}+5B{e}^{4}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=11{e}^{-4},B=-9{e}^{-4}.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =11{e}^{-4}\\cdot {e}^{4x}-9{e}^{-4}\\cdot x{e}^{4x} \\\\  & =11{e}^{4x-4}-9x{e}^{4x-4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386007 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386008 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386007 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386009 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386007 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386010 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386007 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386011 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386007 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386012 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386007 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386007 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386007 1079 #edb/ref 17592186386008 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386007 1080 #uuid "656ffe0f-9fb3-55a1-98b5-b13db8a4f14b" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386008 1081 "y=11{e}^{4x-4}-9x{e}^{4x-4}" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386008 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386008 1084 #uuid "eeaa8919-6cd1-523d-89da-7ef2030fd077" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386009 1081 "y=-7{e}^{4x-4}+9x{e}^{4x-4}" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386009 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386009 1084 #uuid "31ad293a-a2de-5b04-a010-75b1e574916b" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386010 1081 "y=5{e}^{4x-4}-3x{e}^{4x-4}" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386010 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386010 1084 #uuid "0a7466a7-5e6b-57ce