62 17592186045585 true] [17592186386076 1071 "Given the curve  $r(t)=t\\,i+\\sqrt{8}t\\,j-4t\\,k,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=5t,$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386076 1072 #uuid "72f93e03-a33f-50d8-b52b-f8964fad8ff2" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386076 1074 "First, since $s=5t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{5}.$  \n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{s}{5}\\,i+(\\sqrt{8}\\cdot \\frac{s}{5})j-4\\cdot \\frac{s}{5}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{s}{5}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{8}s}{5}\\,j-\\frac{4s}{5}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{5})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{8}s}{5})j-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4s}{5})k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{5}\\,j-\\frac{4}{5}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386077 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386078 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386077 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386079 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386077 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386080 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386077 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386081 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386077 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386082 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386077 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386077 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386077 1079 #edb/ref 17592186386080 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386077 1080 #uuid "c9d079c9-27cf-5f55-a153-92a8cb90ae4d" 13194139