[17592186386167 1069 "q-79485" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386167 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386167 1071 "The position $y(t)$ of a particle oscillating with simple harmonic motion is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+36y=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time, in seconds. What is the period of the oscillation?" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386167 1072 #uuid "3605b04a-15fd-50ac-9f72-ed54fb63e1dd" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386167 1074 "The simple harmonic motion (SHM) equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nIn our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=36\\,⟹\\,\\omega =6.\n$$\n\nThe period $T$ is given by:\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{\\omega }\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, the period (in seconds) is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{6}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\,\\text{s}.\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386168 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386169 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386168 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386170 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386168 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386171 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386168 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386172 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386168 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386173 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386168 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386168 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386168 1079 #edb/ref 17592186386169 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386168 1080 #uuid "c82d1dca-ef4b-58bd-9c92-e1d08b0c6ca2" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386169 1081 "\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\,\\text{s}" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386169 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386169 1084 #uuid "98823c27-20ea-5c80-a076-22a3119126f2" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386170 1081 "\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\,\\text{s}" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386170 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386170 1084 #uuid "cdff06c5-3327-581e-ba27-a81eded2b923" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386171 1081 "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\,\\text{s}" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386171 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386171 1084 #uuid "5568fa4e-4b13-55ba-81d5-48e10bbaa847" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386172 1081 "\\frac{\\pi }{24}\\,\\text{s}" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386172 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386172 1084 #uuid "f0893feb-ede9-5014-9cbd-e1fe1167cac9" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386173 1081 "\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\,\\text{s}" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386173 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386173 1084 #uuid "d772ab1d-81a5-5ceb-8dbf-49c6de2c92f0" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386174 1068 #edb/ref 17592186386175 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386174 1069 "q-79563" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386174 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386174 1071 "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3.$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386174 1072 #uuid "9720bec0-3da4-5217-8468-e4569ac0e63c" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386174 1074 "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =3x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,2.$\n\n![](images/64/64b0962fbb38b2c64da68de01d1c6407174aa66f810b820ece7185866b7f8ff3.png)" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386175 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386176 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386175 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386177 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386175 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386178 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386175 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386179 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386175 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386180 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386175 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386175 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386175 1079 #edb/ref 17592186386180 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386175 1080 #uuid "fe6588a4-c656-5e02-9be8-4235169132b4" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386176 1081 "images/8a/8ac5a8137dd22e9f7333315bc2f5e1120cdb46dc6fb84f938890c491563a86c7.png" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386176 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386176 1084 #uuid "25d0d86d-c06f-5faf-a0ed-e8ee4d8b2010" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386177 1081 "images/f5/f59924b67013ab56263c9e58d283bd29b1869699488702fffc8f88d1de18e647.png" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386177 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386177 1084 #uuid "7cb52152-df73-5351-900a-b8e3c2fe2eee" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386178 1081 "images/41/4110727f4203228259f1ee4d95593e54c92731e986eb3bdcf9cc0692cf902aa4.png" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386178 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386178 1084 #uuid "d01da734-6649-516c-965d-904f6eb30e75" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386179 1081 "images/be/bec2fa9f6c2673fe9bc71fbdadb8f2cbf4c37ef05a38dd2486be3fac7e2b98d2.png" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386179 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386179 1084 #uuid "a9ccb688-6ce7-56f2-8a91-5c430e62080a" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386180 1081 "images/75/757072d5f7b2edaf1eb22e3e1a1c4135a387293396c9a4213ee3a2e213102ee6.png" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386180 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386180 1084 #uuid "b8c43a80-cb88-5719-a3f8-6293badb40f6" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386181 1068 #edb/ref 17592186386182 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386181 1069 "q-79571" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386181 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386181 1071 "The position $y(t)$ of a particle oscillating with light damped harmonic motion is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+8{y}^{′}+41y=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time, in seconds. What is the period of the damped oscillation?" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386181 1072 #uuid "5708124f-9743-5ab7-8b57-9c32436ebfac" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386181 1074 "The given equation represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. We are looking for solutions of the form $y={e}^{\\lambda t}.$\n\nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +41=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +41 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +16)-16+41 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +4)^{2}+25 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +4)^{2} & =-25 \\\\ \\lambda +4 & =\\pm 5\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-4\\pm 5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-4t}(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t).\n$$\n\nFrom the solution, the value of the angular frequency is $Ω=5\\,{\\text{s}}^{-1}.$\n\nThe period of the damped oscillation $T$ is related to the angular frequency as follows:\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{Ω}\n$$\n\nSo the period is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{5}\\,\\text{s}.\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386182 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386183 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386182 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386184 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386182 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386185 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386182 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386186 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386182 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386187 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386182 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386182 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386182 1079 #edb/ref 17592186386185 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386182 1080 #uuid "519ee466-f0d0-576d-b575-b46d45151fdf" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386183 1081 "\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\,\\text{s}" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386183 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386183 1084 #uuid "fa9cb0a8-557e-5b0b-9753-10f618e7048e" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386184 1081 "\\frac{\\pi }{10}\\,\\text{s}" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386184 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386184 1084 #uuid "97d1921f-94da-5b6b-876f-e6446a353e19" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386185 1081 "\\frac{2\\pi }{5}\\,\\text{s}" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386185 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386185 1084 #uuid "b4ce6670-2040-58d6-a375-b175a3d11db9" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386186 1081 "\\frac{4\\pi }{5}\\,\\text{s}" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386186 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386186 1084 #uuid "c1392899-998d-54f1-858c-eece8ca396f9" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386187 1081 "\\frac{\\pi }{20}\\,\\text{s}" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386187 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386187 1084 #uuid "6cbb88df-1a01-5758-84f9-1948b1c83343" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386188 1068 #edb/ref 17592186386189 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386188 1069 "q-79620" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386188 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386188 1071 "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n{t}^{2}{y}^{″}+4t{y}^{′}+2y={e}^{t},\\,t>0\n$$\n\nhas the complimentary function ${y}_{c}(t)=\\frac{A}{t}+\\frac{B}{{t}^{2}}$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(t)$ to this equation. \n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:* \n\n$$\n\\int t{e}^{t}\\text{d}t=(t-1){e}^{t}+C\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386188 1072 #uuid "1bb8ed71-56ab-536b-a7bf-0caa82667de7" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386188 1074 "First, we reduce the differential equation to the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(t){y}^{′}+Q(t)y=f(t).\n$$\n\nSo, we divide both sides of the given equation by ${t}^{2}.$ We get\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+\\frac{4}{t}{y}^{′}+\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}y=\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nWe notice that the forcing term $f(t)=\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}{e}^{t}.$ Additionally, we're given the fundamental solutions:\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(t)=\\frac{1}{t},\\,{y}_{2}(t)=\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute the Wronskian:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W({y}_{1},{y}_{2}) & =|\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{′} & {y}_{2}^{′}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={y}_{1}{y}_{2}^{′}-{y}_{1}^{′}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}{(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}})}^{′}-{(\\frac{1}{t})}^{′}\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}(-\\frac{2}{{t}^{3}})-(-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}})\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{t}^{4}}+\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the Wronskian is not equal to zero, this confirms that the functions  ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ are independent. \n\nAccording to the method of variation of parameters, the particular solution of the differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}(t) & ={y}_{1}(t)u(t)+{y}_{2}(t)v(t),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =-\\int \\frac{f(t){y}_{2}(t)}{W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})}\\,\\text{d}t=\\int {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t={e}^{t}, \\\\ v(t) & =\\int \\frac{f(t){y}_{1}(t)}{W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})}\\,\\text{d}t=-\\int t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t=(1-t){e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}(t) & ={y}_{1}(t)u(t)+{y}_{2}(t)v(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\cdot {e}^{t}+\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\cdot (1-t){e}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}{e}^{t}+(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{t}){e}^{t} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{t}+\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{t}){e}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}{e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386189 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386190 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386189 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386191 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386189 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386192 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386189 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386193 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386189 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386194 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386189 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386189 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386189 1079 #edb/ref 17592186386190 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386189 1080 #uuid "8de45fec-6d7a-5cbb-8c75-d5637ebdb1b3" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386190 1081 "{y}_{p}(t)=\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}{e}^{t}" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386190 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386190 1084 #uuid "ea4d47ac-28b7-5cf4-9951-7b77a964f98a" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386191 1081 "{y}_{p}(t)=(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{t}){e}^{t}" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386191 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386191 1084 #uuid "cf86acff-f5b4-55bc-b223-41ec5c107c1f" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386192 1081 "{y}_{p}(t