}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}-4y+1 & 3{y}^{2}-4x-1\\end{aligned}],$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-4y+1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=3{y}^{2}-4x-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-4y+1)=0\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{y}^{2}-4x-1)=-4 \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-4y+1)=-4\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{y}^{2}-4x-1)=6y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 6y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386354 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386355 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386354 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386356 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386354 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386357 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386354 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386358 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386354 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386359 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386354 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386354 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386354 1079 #edb/ref 17592186386355 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386354 1080 #uuid "0b5b2192-3f70-59ee-87fd-c98b6a39c105" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386355 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 6y\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386355 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045