ype I region. \n\n- To determine the $x$-limits, we need to find the $x$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x} & =e \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x$-limits are \n$0\\le x\\le 1.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](images/95/95a6d9b0bc464c719311dc900967ebd06a3aa3d3004cfe5303359eecb20551e7.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{e}^{x}\\le y\\le e}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{e}^{x}}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386396 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386397 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386396 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386398 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386396 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386399 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386396 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386400 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386396 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386401 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386396 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386396 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386396 1079 #edb/ref 17592186386398 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386396 1080 #uuid "16108ca6-d4a1-58ab-98a0-df70a7ed9b7d" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386397 1081 "{\\int }_{{e}^{x}}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386397 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386397 1084 #uuid "4fbf96df-a77e-53bb-b04a-f2a56751b43b" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386398 1081 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{e}^{x}}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [1759218