ligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}r & 0 \\\\ 0 & r\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, in order to find $Av$, we need to rotate $v$ counterclockwise by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$  and scale the result by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{3},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/fd/fd2fda4038ae2342b37df91a520a58463ce70748c143c6619968da71411aff1c.png)" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386498 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386498 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386500 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386498 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386501 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386498 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386502 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386498 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386503 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386498 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386498 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386498 1079 #edb/ref 17592186386502 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386498 1080 #uuid "e51414d9-147d-5c81-b876-34c3bdd3b99b" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386499 1081 "images/9f/9f2b2163f62915ab2a88d96b2e9c40fa1ef5db3f869df495dfd92ac839c5cb2c.png" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386499 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533