}^{2}.$ \nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to S}$ from $B$ to $S$ if \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386532 1072 #uuid "62dadad6-bc72-59c3-b335-faab5922669e" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386532 1074 "Recall  that the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ consists of the vectors ${e}_{1}$ and ${e}_{2},$ given by\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe components of the vectors of $B$ are just the coordinates relative to the standard basis:\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{2}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $S.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 11\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386533 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386534 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386533 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386535 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386533 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386536 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386533 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386537 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386533 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386538 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386533 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386533 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386533 1079 #edb/ref 17592186386536 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386533 1080 #uuid "8055db6f-b8ff-53ba-9dfb-f141126526ea" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386534 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 5\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386534 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386534 1084 #uuid "e0f2de09-e3ad-512b-8e74-3a12edf3480d" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386535 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 11 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386535 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386535 1084 #uuid "1fcb9a14-b5a6-5c03-9ec6-27fac7199ae9" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386536 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 11\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386536 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386536 1084 #uuid "9f078de7-6bf2-52c5-bbfd-2095ee4f5399" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386537 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 11\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386537 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386537 1084 #uuid "76983eb3-ee3b-59df-9616-86db07326c79" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386538 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 11 & 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386538 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386538 1084 #uuid "9158d772-d565-5842-972a-4024fc2947d3" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386539 1068 #edb/ref 17592186386540 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386539 1069 "q-81848" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386539 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386539 1071 "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{3}.$ What are the values of $a,b,$ and $c$ if \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is \n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & a & -3 \\\\