[(¬X⇒¬Y)∧(¬Y⇒¬X)]\n$$\n\nNow, we represent all the implications using disjunctions and negations:\n\n$$\n¬[(¬X⇒¬Y)∧(¬Y⇒¬X)]≡¬[(¬¬X∨¬Y)∧(¬¬Y∨¬X)]\n$$\n\nNext, we simplify the double negations:\n\n$$\n¬[(¬¬X∨¬Y)∧(¬¬Y∨¬X)]≡¬[(X∨¬Y)∧(Y∨¬X)]\n$$\n\nNext, we use De Morgan's laws:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬[(X∨¬Y)∧(Y∨¬X)] & ≡¬(X∨¬Y)∨¬(Y∨¬X) \\\\  & ≡(¬X∧¬¬Y)∨(¬Y∧¬¬X)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we again simplify the double negations:\n\n$$\n(¬X∧¬¬Y)∨(¬Y∧¬¬X)≡(¬X∧Y)∨(¬Y∧X)\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386718 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386719 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386718 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386720 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386718 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386721 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386718 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386722 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386718 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386723 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386718 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386718 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386718 1079 #edb/ref 17592186386722 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386718 1080 #uuid "f1c55f37-dfa2-5f45-acd3-4ca2d5a301de" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386719 1081 "¬(X∨Y)∧X" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386719 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386719 1084 #uuid "c8e0c462-bed9-534d-a8c4-881399656916" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386720 1081 "(¬X∧Y)⇒(¬Y∧X)" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386720 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386720 1084 #uuid "b4ba4e7d-b859-5bc6-9152-a638404dd6cd" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386721 1081 "X⇔Y" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386721 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386721 1084 #uuid "9a50d2ad-fe71-5ee1-9903-848ed5950674" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386722 1081 "(¬X∧Y)∨(¬Y∧X)" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386722 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386722 1084 #uuid "b8f73c55-ed3b-50d8-b759-f68ddf443173" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386723 1081 "(X∨¬Y)∧(Y∨¬X)" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386723 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386723 1084 #uuid "73b69ceb-20b1-5829-8db9-c8f84923f153" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386724 1068 #edb/ref 17592186386725 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386724 1069 "q-83228" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386724 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386724 1071 "$¬(A⇔¬B)≡$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386724 1072 #uuid "1d70dc23-0b2b-583b-a868-4b96eea33478" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386724 1074 "First, we use the definition of the biconditional statement to write the equivalence as a conjunction of implications: \n\n$$\n¬(A⇔¬B)≡¬[(A⇒¬B)∧(¬B⇒A)]\n$$\n\nNow, we represent all the implications using disjunctions and negations:\n\n$$\n¬[(A⇒¬B)∧(¬B⇒A)]≡¬[(¬A∨¬B)∧(¬¬B∨A)]\n$$\n\nNext, we use De Morgan's laws:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬[(¬A∨¬B)∧(¬¬B∨A)] & ≡¬(¬A∨¬B)∨¬(¬¬B∨A) \\\\  & ≡(¬¬A∧¬¬B)∨(¬¬¬B∧¬A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the double negations:\n\n$$\n(¬¬A∧¬¬B)∨(¬¬¬B∧¬A)≡(A∧B)∨(¬B∧¬A)\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386725 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386726 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386725 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386727 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386725 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386728 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386725 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386729 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386725 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386730 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386725 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386725 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386725 1079 #edb/ref 17592186386726 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386725 1080 #uuid "308b1036-f48b-5cc5-8e4e-84a06172ed0a" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386726 1081 "(A∧B)∨(¬B∧¬A)" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386726 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386726 1084 #uuid "3a684d45-6b63-5dd8-b9a5-e442bc750b36" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386727 1081 "¬A⇔B" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386727 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386727 1084 #uuid "3f3ca549-f6ca-53d9-b8c4-f23c9f8b743f" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386728 1081 "¬(A∧¬B)∨B" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386728 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386728 1084 #uuid "72275d9a-5691-5409-9a91-f5d269c7967d" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386729 1081 "(A∧B)⇒(¬B∧A)" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386729 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386729 1084 #uuid "63457471-ee36-5ea2-8284-ec13d0df36fc" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386730 1081 "(¬A∧B)∧(¬B∨¬A)" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386730 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386730 1084 #uuid "b4473d7d-850c-5f8a-8ff6-0eae0ce8c33c" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386731 1068 #edb/ref 17592186386732 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386731 1069 "q-83497" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386731 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386731 1071 "The acceleration $a$ at time $t$ of a particle $P$ moving in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\na(t)=⟨12(1+2t)^{3},9(1-3t)^{2}⟩.\n$$\n\nGiven that the particle has velocity $v=⟨1,6⟩$ when $t=0,$ calculate the velocity vector of $P$ at time $t=1.$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386731 1072 #uuid "cb1ed2a5-10d4-520a-8be1-03271b56ffd4" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386731 1074 "To compute the velocity vector, we need to integrate the acceleration vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨12(1+2t)^{3},9(1-3t)^{2}⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int 12(1+2t)^{3}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 9(1-3t)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3}{2}(1+2t)^{4}+{C}_{1},\\,-(1-3t)^{3}+{C}_{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $v(0)=⟨1,6⟩.$ Substituting $t=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(0) & =⟨\\frac{3}{2}(1+2(0))^{4}+{C}_{1},\\,-(1-3(0))^{3}+{C}_{2}⟩ \\\\ ⟨1,6⟩ & =⟨\\frac{3}{2}+{C}_{1},\\,-1+{C}_{2}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso we must have ${C}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and ${C}_{2}=7.$ Therefore, the velocity is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =⟨\\frac{3}{2}(1+2t)^{4}-\\frac{1}{2},\\,-(1-3t)^{3}+7⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the velocity at time $t=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =⟨\\frac{3}{2}(1+2(1))^{4}-\\frac{1}{2},\\,-(1-3(1))^{3}+7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨121,15⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386732 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386733 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386732 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386734 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386732 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386735 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386732 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386736 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386732 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386737 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386732 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386732 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386732 1079 #edb/ref 17592186386733 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386732 1080 #uuid "51f50a45-adc6-5b16-876f-809ec791c11f" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386733 1081 "v(1)=⟨121,15⟩" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [175921863