\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can find the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{x}$ of the equation above by solving the corresponding normal equation, which we obtain by left-multiplying our original equation by ${A}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\overset{^}{x} & ={A}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is invertible. Therefore, multiplying by $({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}$ on the left, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{x} & =({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}{A}^{T}b \\\\  & ={([\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386952 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386953 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386952 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386954 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386952 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386955 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386952 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386956 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386952 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386957 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386952 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386952 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386952 1079 #edb/ref 17592